-## Independently reviewable stages
-
-| Stage | Change | Acceptance gate |
-|---|---|---|
-| 1 | Exclude pure evaluation from the training execution cursor | Existing eager MoE train/eval/train and clipping parity |
-| 2 | Preserve the native v2 checkpoint layout | SwiGLU EP1/2/4 save/load roundtrips and normal pretraining restart |
-| 3 | Add scoped capture lifecycle and fixed gathered-buffer addresses | Partial-scope attention/MLA loss, gradient, main-weight, and Adam-state parity; failure cleanup; teardown |
-| 4 | Validate MoE composition in normal training | Real text, multiple accumulated microbatches, evaluation, DCP save/load, graph recapture after restart |
-| 5 | Measure performance and memory | Matched eager baseline, AB/BA repeats, capture cost, steady-state step time, allocated/reserved peak memory, GPU activity monitoring |
-
-Stages 1 and 2 are small prerequisite fixes. Stage 3 has the highest correctness
-risk because hook execution, graph autograd, stream ordering, and buffer lifetime
-must agree. Stage 4 prevents successful capture from masking a broken training
-composition. Stage 5 must be assessed separately. Measurements on a shared
-host describe that environment and must identify other resident GPU contexts;
-repeat on dedicated GPUs before generalizing performance gains.
